{"ts": 1791260096.862234, "type": "step", "step": 21, "action": "messages_read_channel", "args": {"channel": "dm:student"}, "output": "[t=-10] student: hey, I started the writeup but I'm stuck on the eval part\n[t=0] agent: I\u2019m going to check the Week 3 reading and your draft, then help you turn the eval section into something concrete. Usually for this build, eval means explaining how you measure success and reporting pass^k over multiple seeds.\n[t=0] student: ok got it, thanks\n[t=6] agent: Let\u2019s fix the eval section first. Please read the short section I just assigned on pass@k vs pass^k, then send me in 1\u20132 sentences: (1) what pass^k means, and (2) why the instructor might prefer it for this build.\n[t=6] student: nice, I think I see it now", "t": 8, "activity": [], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.27998147170370613, "pomdp": 0.27998147170370613, "pass_k": 0.49811695777512915}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.8296771462848964, "motivation": 0.8330753570864192, "reliance": 0.32481971324228814, "persistence": 0.48938443592806424, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3136352668677162, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2892105949863653, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 1.7, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791260098.727572, "type": "step", "step": 22, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Great \u2014 then say it in your own words: reply with one sentence completing this frame: \u201cI use pass^k because ____.\u201d After that, we\u2019ll turn it directly into your Evaluation paragraph.", "intent": "hint", "concept": "week3_eval"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: ok got it, thanks\n[activity] t=8 messages 2m", "t": 10, "activity": [{"t": 8, "app": "messages", "minutes": 2, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.27998147170370613, "pomdp": 0.27998147170370613, "pass_k": 0.5257621870472421}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.8296771462848964, "motivation": 0.8330753570864192, "reliance": 0.34481971324228816, "persistence": 0.48938443592806424, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3136352668677162, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2892105949863653, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.19, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791260101.258345, "type": "step", "step": 23, "action": "notes_append", "args": {"note_id": "writeup", "text": "\n## Evaluation scaffold\nUse this structure for the eval section:\n- Metric: We evaluate reliability with pass^k, where a run counts as passing only if all k evaluation attempts succeed.\n- Why this metric: pass^k is stricter than pass@k and better matches whether the system works reliably, not just occasionally.\n- Setup: Report results on at least 3 seeds, as required by the instructor.\n- What to report: the task/check used, the number of attempts per seed, and the observed pass^k across seeds.\n"}, "output": "Appended.", "t": 10, "activity": [], "events": [{"type": "note_edit", "note_id": "writeup", "by": "agent"}], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.27998147170370613, "pomdp": 0.27998147170370613, "pass_k": 0.5257621870472421}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.8296771462848964, "motivation": 0.8330753570864192, "reliance": 0.34481971324228816, "persistence": 0.48938443592806424, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3136352668677162, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2892105949863653, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.19, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791260103.457292, "type": "step", "step": 24, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Good start. Next, I want to check whether you can apply the metric, not just name it. Reply with a concrete example: if you test 3 seeds and each seed has 2 evaluation attempts, what would count as pass^2 for a seed? And what result pattern would show weak reliability even if pass@2 looks good?", "intent": "hint", "concept": "week3_eval"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: makes sense. what next?\n[activity] t=10 messages 2m", "t": 12, "activity": [{"t": 10, "app": "messages", "minutes": 2, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.27998147170370613, "pomdp": 0.27998147170370613, "pass_k": 0.5831089447482768}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.8296771462848964, "motivation": 0.8330753570864192, "reliance": 0.3648197132422882, "persistence": 0.48938443592806424, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3136352668677162, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2892105949863653, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.533, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
